{
	"about": [
		"Exchanges. A session is new, authenticated as device \"d1\" of app \"todo\", or a link session (authenticated as the server-kind device \"s1\", with no app). With the backend in the state given, a client call sends the client frame (and clientBody, if any); the server answers with the server frames (and serverBody); the call resolves with result or fails with the error code. push is a changed frame the server sends unasked; pushApps is an apps frame and pushDevices a devices frame the server sends unasked.",
		"closes: the server closes the channel after its frames. An error frame also carries a message, English text for a developer whose wording is the server's; it is not compared.",
		"Bodies are UTF-8 text. backend keys: welcome, helloError, paired, pairError, head, doc, put ({stored} or {conflict}), putError, apps, appsError, devices, announceError. A welcome result holds role and subordinates when the frame carries them.",
		"exchanges are spoken by every client. serverKind holds the exchanges of a server-kind device: a subordinate server linking to its main. The client package does not speak them; the server's Session and its Go client play them.",
		"tolerated: frames one side accepts although the other side never sends them."
	],
